  "implementation": [
    "Finite bounded native-point preference and one searchable native numeric field/stepper; 54 unique Settings entries.",
    "Spacing uses disposable paragraph copies and reversible native default/typing styles. Existing backing attributes, view identity, source, revision, selection and history are preserved.",
    "Zero-spacing default retains the original native paragraph path unless backing metadata carries older nonzero spacing. No explicit offscreen layout is forced by the preference refresh.",
    "Defer spacing and typing geometry while marked text is active/being received; simulated Japanese and Chinese preedit attributes and model source remain unchanged.",
    "Public NSTextView rectangle overrides correct only the empty terminal insertion at managed nonzero spacing, using cached native font line height and the native bottom edge. No private selector or attached TextKit 1 manager.",
    "Preview input is reported before its coalesced scroll report. Native moves carry generation, revision and preview/source input sequences; stale queued moves and late reports cannot reclaim newer input. Zoom completion respects newer source gestures."
  ],
  "tests": [
    "Original-key migration, explicit zero/fractional reopen, search and finite bounds.",
    "Native row distances, wrapped/cached offscreen paragraphs, themed and unthemed paths at zoom 0.5/1/2.",
    "Native-reference terminal caret height AND local X/Y across empty/Tail/LF/CRLF, spacing 3/100 and zoom 0.5/1/2; reset/undo and TextKit 2 remain intact.",
    "Simulated Japanese/Chinese composition defers spacing while preserving preedit attributes and document revision.",
    "One main-actor turn queues preview input followed by a stale native movement; preview stays at 2200 and source follows, then native PageDown takes control. No timeout increase.",
    "19 compiled app UI methods; new test types 12.5 in Settings, checks persistence, exact mixed-list source and native undo/redo, restores zero; screenshot attachments for settings, source selection and terminal caret."
